<title>USA: Centralia, Pa., tax bills shift to state amid fire.</title>
<headline>Centralia, Pa., tax bills shift to state amid fire.</headline>
<dateline>CENTRALIA, Pa. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials in Columbia County, Pa., transferred all of Centralia's property tax bills to the state as a fire burning under the town for the past 30 years continued to smolder.</p>
<p>The state condemned the property in 1992 because of the fire, which is burning in an abandoned coal mine.</p>
<p>A total of $42 million has been spent on relocating residents, and county officials said there are still about 20 families living atop the fire who are continuing to pay property taxes.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
